<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arthur St. Clair</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1737–1818</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arthur St. Clair (1737–1818) was a Scottish-born American soldier and politician who served as a general in the Revolutionary War, as president of the Confederation Congress in 1787 and as first governor of the Northwest Territory. In November 1791 his army was routed near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wabash-river">Wabash River</a> by the Western Confederacy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-turtle">Little Turtle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-jacket">Blue Jacket</a>, the worst defeat ever suffered by the US Army against Native Americans.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arthur-st-clair.jpg" alt="Arthur St. Clair" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Willson Peale · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ArthurStClairOfficialPortrait-restored.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
